      "content": "i mean i get that it's a gray area, but isn't it kind of a false equivalence? like, if a country uses sanctions to stop a regime from committing human rights abuses, that's clearly different from just bullying someone for no reason. shouldn't we say that sanctions are an essential tool for international justice when they're used the right way?",
